  "body": "Fork synced at v0.17.0 (branched from upstream/main f490458a).\n\n## What changed\n- **`machining3d::hsm::plan_level`**: every arm that hands an Adaptive level to the Offset rings now goes through one helper, `rings_named`. These arms are: a level the seam crosses, a narrowed helix on the wrap, a hard planner refusal on the wrap, and `adaptive_passes`' own fallback. The helper writes `<why> - Offset rings cut <level> instead`, with the level named by its Z, or by its developed radius on the wrap. The text of every note is unchanged. A guard was added: if the planner ever hands back rings without a note naming the level, `plan_level` adds one. Toolpaths and verdicts do not change. Only notes are affected, and only if that guard ever fires.\n- **The reported case was a test-reader artifact.** I reproduced \"radius 5.6 cut by rings, no note\" on #882's held commit 70ac996f with `INSET = 0` (the \"0.25 um thinning\" variant). It is not a planner fallback. The 5.0 level's microlift lifts to 5.6, and one down ramp runs 5.7 -> 5.6 -> 5.5 with a vertex on 5.6. The rotary_adaptive reader counted any plane that a descent ends on as a cut level. It therefore read the lifted runs as a level with 7 planar moves, no arcs and no load. The reader (`rotary_adaptive_fixture::read_levels`) now reads only the ladder's own planes (`top - k * stepdown`) and takes the stepdown as an argument.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/983-rings-fallback-note.md`. It covers why rest and shell passes keep their single note, and why the r6.2 travel pin was left alone (its flip is #982's microlift-acceptance knife edge).\n\n## How tested (local, macOS, debug unless noted)\n- New pins: `machining3d::hsm::fallback_tests::{a_developed_level_the_planner_refuses_is_named_by_its_radius, a_planar_level_the_planner_refuses_is_named_by_its_z, a_developed_level_the_seam_cuts_is_named_by_its_radius}` and `rotary_adaptive::a_microlift_plane_is_not_read_as_an_unnamed_ring_level`.\n- motion lib: 192 passed. adaptive_hsm 1, adaptive_band 2, pocket3d_hsm (motion) 3, rotary_adaptive 3: all pass.\n- Release `--ignored`: adaptive_hsm 5/5, rotary_adaptive 3/3. adaptive_band has no ignored tests.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Repro check: on #882's held commit with `INSET = 0` and this PR's reader, the phantom 5.6 level is gone and all three rotary heavy tests pass.\n\n## Not exercised\n- App and UI suites: no note text changed, so nothing reads differently there. The app `pocket3d_hsm` bore heavy test is #984's and was not run.\n- The new guard cannot fire on any current path; it is defensive and has no test that drives it.\n\nOverlaps: none with #953 (grow.rs not touched), #982 or #882.\n\nChangelog: none (notes-only refactor plus a test-reader fix; no output change)\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #983\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
